From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 04:33:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: do not force PROT_EXEC on iOS for ProcessExecuteFlags

Wine's loader turns on ProcessExecuteFlags MEM_EXECUTE_OPTION_ENABLE for
a main executable without IMAGE_DLLCHARACTERISTICS_NX_COMPAT, and
virtual_set_force_exec then asks mprotect for PROT_EXEC with every
PROT_READ. iOS never grants that outside the JIT pool, so mprotect_exec
returned -1 for every read-only request, and NtProtectVirtualMemory
returned STATUS_ACCESS_DENIED. Mortal Kombat Komplete Edition's MKKE.exe
(i386, DllCharacteristics 0x8000) died in its WoW64 start: wow64.dll's
import table was restored to read-only after binding, the restore
failed before the pool copy was synced, and wow64.dll's first import
call jumped to the import's RVA:

  [vmem-denied] set_vprot failed: base=0x73fdaf3000 size=0x1000 protect=0x2
  [mach_exc] UNHANDLED #1 pc=0x34f4c addr=0x34f4c ... lr PE: wow64.dll+0x1d0f4

Guest code runs through FEX, which keeps EXEC in Wine's logical vprot,
and force_exec_prot is one flag for every pseudo-process in the one
Mach process, so on iOS the flags are recorded but the host protection
is left alone.

Class: ios-port
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-09-mkke-force-exec.md
Offered-upstream: no; Madeira's iOS port
---
 build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c b/build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c
index be373c6..fa83eb8 100644
--- a/build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c
+++ b/build/ntdll-unix/process_ios.c
@@ -2798,7 +2798,20 @@ NTSTATUS WINAPI NtSetInformationProcess( HANDLE handle, PROCESSINFOCLASS class,
                 return STATUS_INVALID_PARAMETER;
             }
             execute_flags = *(ULONG *)info;
+#ifdef WINE_IOS
+            /* Forced PROT_EXEC cannot be had on iOS: mprotect never grants
+             * EXEC outside the JIT pool, so with it every later read-only
+             * mprotect failed (NtProtectVirtualMemory c0000022). Guest code
+             * runs through FEX, which keeps EXEC in Wine's logical vprot,
+             * and the flag is one for every pseudo-process here. The
+             * loader sets it for a main executable without NX_COMPAT
+             * (Mortal Kombat Komplete Edition's i386 MKKE.exe): wow64.dll's
+             * import table then stayed unsynced to its pool copy, and its
+             * first import call jumped to an RVA. */
+            (void)enable;
+#else
             virtual_set_force_exec( enable );
+#endif
         }
         break;
 
